WEBVTT

00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:06.140
What is the one goal, if you achieved it in the next 90 days,

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:10.600
would fundamentally change your game as a leader?

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:14.600
The 90-Day Way is a time-bound leadership operating system.

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:16.560
Before you can guide your team,

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:20.600
before you can create a plan for them, you must create your own.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:26.600
This forces you to get clear on your priorities, identify your own roadblocks,

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:30.600
and model the very focus you expect from your team.

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:36.600
A manager I coach felt perpetually behind. Her 90-day goal wasn't about a project.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.600
It was about her leadership.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:44.310
Her goal? Delegate one significant responsibility to a high-potential

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:49.600
team member to free up five hours a week for strategic thinking.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:53.600
It was specific, measurable, and transformational.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:59.600
Your play is to use the template in your playbook to draft your own 90-day plan.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:03.640
You'll see it starts with space for your M.V.P.

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:07.600
and a quick assessment of your Core 4 pillars.

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:10.950
This ensures your goals are grounded in your

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:14.600
purpose and focus on the areas you want to grow.

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:20.600
Focus on one single high-impact goal for yourself as a leader.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:22.600
You've set your 90-day goal.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:26.720
Now identify one roadblock, the distraction,

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:31.600
habit, or meeting that is most likely to derail you.

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:38.600
And ask yourself, which of your Core 4 pillars will this roadblock test the most?

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:44.600
Is it a test of your resilience, your agility, your alignment, your wellbeing?

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:47.600
Understanding this helps you prepare.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:50.600
What is your plan to neutralize it?

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:56.600
To capture your thinking, turn to the roadblock neutralizer drill in your playbook.

00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:58.960
Once you have your own plan in place,

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:02.600
we'll focus on how to introduce this system to your team.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:04.600
I'll see you in the next video.
